# Day 16-17 Summary: Admin Dashboard and Frontend-Backend Integration



## Goal
Give admins their own dashboard to review and act on every resource request, connected to the live FastAPI backend.

## What was built
1. **Admin dashboard page** (`pages/AdminDashboard.jsx`, `pages/admin.css`)
   - Sidebar layout: Overview, My requests, New request, logged-in email, Log out.
   - Six status cards (pending, approved, provisioning, provisioned, rejected, failed) with live counts. Clicking a card filters the table.
   - SVG donut chart of requests by status (no chart library).
   - Requests table (ID, user, instance, OS, cost, status) with a status filter dropdown.
   - Row actions, shown only when valid for the status: Approve and Reject (asks for a reason) on pending, Provision on approved.
   - Loading and error messages, and horizontal scroll for the table on small screens.
2. **Admin route guard** (`components/AdminRoute.jsx`): not logged in goes to /login, a non-admin goes to /dashboard, an admin sees /admin.
3. **Routing** (`App.jsx`): added `/admin`. App.jsx now holds routes only. BrowserRouter and AuthProvider stay in main.jsx.
4. **Login redirect** (`Login.jsx`): admins go to /admin, users go to /dashboard.

## API endpoints used
- GET /requests (admins receive all requests)
- PATCH /requests/{id}/approve
- PATCH /requests/{id}/reject (body: reason)
- PATCH /requests/{id}/start-provisioning

## Problems met and fixes
| Problem | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| "Already included file name ... differs only in casing" | File saved as Admindashboard.jsx and AdminDashboard.css | Renamed to AdminDashboard.jsx and admin.css, then Reload Window |
| "Cannot render a Router inside another Router" | BrowserRouter in both main.jsx and App.jsx | App.jsx now contains only Routes |
| "A module cannot have multiple default exports" | New App code pasted below the old code | Replaced the whole file via a PowerShell here-string |
| 403 on GET /requests/6 | Opened a request the logged-in account does not own | Expected backend behavior; admins can open any request |
| Admin landed on /dashboard | Login.jsx redirect line not yet changed | One-line change to role-based navigate |

## Result
- /admin shows live data: 6 requests (4 provisioning, 2 rejected, 0 pending).
- Route protection works for admins and regular users.

